<%# The channel banner: what you are watching, on what channel, at what time.

    Built to look like the thing it is imitating -- a bevelled bar with the channel in a
    lit-up badge at one end and a direction pad at the other. The pad is the whole of the
    controls now: the ring of icons the watch page uses belongs to a page you work through,
    and this is a television.

    The arrows do two different jobs, which is how they were on the box too. Up and down
    change the channel, and are ordinary cinema-move links. Left and right change nothing at
    all -- they walk the banner along this channel's running order so you can see what you
    missed and what is coming, and it falls back to what is actually on after a moment. %>
<div class="cable-hud"
     data-controller="cable-hud"
     data-cable-hud-showing-class="cable-hud--peeking">

  <%# The channel, in the corner the number always sat in. %>
  <a class="cable-hud__badge" href="<%= list_path(channel) %>" title="Open <%= channel.name %>">
    <span class="cable-hud__set">
      <span class="cable-hud__aerial"></span>
      <span class="cable-hud__number"><%= number %></span>
    </span>
  </a>

  <div class="cable-hud__body">
    <%# The channel's own page. The badge leads to the same place -- one is the number you
        look at, the other the name you read, and both are the channel. %>
    <a class="cable-hud__channel" href="<%= list_path(channel) %>"><%= channel.name %></a>

    <%# The programme, and it is a link out of cable -- the same pair the guide's panel
        offers: the channel to its own page, the title to the ordinary watch player, where
        it plays from the beginning and counts towards what you have seen. %>
    <a class="cable-hud__title" data-cable-hud-target="title" href="#"></a>
    <p class="cable-hud__context" data-cable-hud-target="context"></p>
    <p class="cable-hud__meta">
      <span class="cable-hud__when" data-cable-hud-target="when"></span>
      <span class="cable-hud__label" data-cable-hud-target="label"></span>
    </p>
  </div>

  <%# Up and down tune; left and right only look. The two kinds are deliberately the same
      shape, because on the remote they were. %>
  <div class="cable-hud__pad">
    <%= link_to cable_channel_path(CableSchedule.sibling(channel, :previous)),
                class: "cable-hud__key cable-hud__key--up", title: "Channel up",
                data: { cinema_move: true } do %>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-caret-up"></i>
    <% end %>

    <button type="button" class="cable-hud__key cable-hud__key--left"
            title="What was on before" data-action="click->cable-hud#earlier">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-caret-left"></i>
    </button>

    <%# The middle of the pad, where SEL was. The one thing on this page that writes
        anything, and only when somebody presses it. %>
    <span class="cable-hud__sel">
      <% if user %>
        <%= render 'entries/completion_status', entry: entry, user: user, minimal: true %>
      <% end %>
    </span>

    <button type="button" class="cable-hud__key cable-hud__key--right"
            title="What is on next" data-action="click->cable-hud#later">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-caret-right"></i>
    </button>

    <%= link_to cable_channel_path(CableSchedule.sibling(channel, :next)),
                class: "cable-hud__key cable-hud__key--down", title: "Channel down",
                data: { cinema_move: true, cinema_preload: true } do %>
      <i class="fa-solid fa-caret-down"></i>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%= link_to root_path, class: "cable-hud__home", title: "Home" do %>
    <i class="fa-solid fa-house"></i>
  <% end %>

  <%# The running order the arrows walk, rendered rather than fetched: it is a handful of
      rows the page already had, and the arrows should answer instantly. Hidden because it
      is data, not a list anybody reads here -- the guide is where you read one. %>
  <div class="cable-hud__schedule" hidden data-cable-hud-target="schedule">
    <% nearby.each do |slot| %>
      <span data-slot-start="<%= (slot.starts_at.to_f * 1000).round %>"
            data-slot-end="<%= (slot.ends_at.to_f * 1000).round %>"
            data-slot-title="<%= cable_programme_headline(slot) %>"
            data-slot-context="<%= cable_programme_context(slot) %>"
            data-slot-url="<%= watch_entry_path(slot.entry, channel: channel.id,
                                                subentry: slot.subentry&.id) %>"
            data-slot-current="<%= slot.id == current_slot.id %>"></span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
